## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides; tier 2, so short)
- **G-1 delta (C1).** A path beyond the one, a product, package or config byte = **Blocker**; any removed line, an old row changed or loosened = **Major, class (d)**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or the commit message = **Blocker**; a second commit or a moved head = STOP; a Jira key or work number in an added line or the commit message = **Minor**; non-ASCII or a tab in the added lines = **Major**.
- **G-2 the rows against mutants (C2).** *Classification rule:* a shape is **IN the family** when it makes the first separator, the second separator or the fourth year character accept an underscore (any spelling, any wider class that holds `_`); it is **OUT** when it takes only a character other than `_`, an underscore at the first, second or third year character, the month or day classes, a flag or a line-break value. For an IN shape: not red on a new row (or red on an old row too: the shape was not green on the old file, a **Note** with the cell) = **Major, class (a)**; a closed-list id (C2b SEP*, SEPDIG*) not red on a named new row = **Major, class (a)**; a predicted-equivalent id (MDIG, DDIG, EQ09) red = the equivalence claim is wrong, **Major** with the measurement; a new row red at main's product = **Major, class (c)**; a new row green under the defect its title names, or red only as a thrown error = **Major, class (b)**; an old-file red set not a subset of the new = **Major**; a regression id no longer red on the rows that were red = **Major**; a control that cannot fail (c2, c4, c5) = the run is DEAD (say so, NOT TESTED) and for c4 a **Major** of its own. For an OUT shape green on all 37 = **Note** with ticket text and the measurement, **even when the route stores a date or answers 500** (YP1-YP3: the builder reports them green; say what the route does), a decision for Tuesday (three more rows `"_027-01-01"`, `"2_27-01-01"`, `"20_7-01-01"`), not a reason for NO GO round 1 (the commission's lane names the two edits and the full class).
- **G-3 counts and CI (C3, C4).** The file other than 37 of 37, or the group other than main + 0 files + 3 tests, without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 3 = **Major**; lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head and zero on main = **Major**; a whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); a failing check-run on the head = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional); an open alert on the PR ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the `contract.ts(23,1) TS2349` error of the scratch typecheck (an untouched file), the unit chain's one explicit-run skip.
- **G-4 words (C5, C7).** A commit-message sentence a run does not carry = **Major (class e)**; a PR title or body sentence a run does not carry = **Minor** (Tuesday edits it); a title that claims more than its rows assert: **Minor** when the overclaim is wording only and the one row it names does assert its own claim (the `describe` and the year `it` tail say "a digit of the year" while the row sends the fourth place only), **Major, class (b)** only if a Done-when shape of the ticket is green; a builder claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number; a survivor outside the family = **Note** in FOR TUESDAY with the value that does it, not of the class.
- **G-5 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker or any Major of the class = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (with cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch; a second NO GO on this class is a STOP to Tuesday under the cap). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` (list the Deferred rows; decisions in FOR TUESDAY). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional. A PR title or body wording is Tuesday's edit before landing, never a reason by itself to send the branch back. **Tier handoff (G2 to G1):** a Major whose consequence is "another target" or "silently applies other content" goes to Tuesday as a STOP-with-measurement rather than a quiet NO GO; here, an underscore date the route STORES (SEP1 family: `2027_01-01` stored as `2027-01-01`) is the ticket's own shape and is NOT a handoff; a survivor of your own IN-family that stores a value the ticket's shapes do not is.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 6.91 at the draft: other seats are live). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, the `apps/api` group, any vitest over more than one file, the unit chain, the mutant battery. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the clone, C4 polls, C5/C6/C7 reads). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b864/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b864/quarantine/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b864/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line. Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b864-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b864-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`; `npm ci` must be CACHED); record node, npm, vitest, tsc (RELAYED by the builder: node v22.23.2, npm 10.9.8, vitest 5.0.0, tsc 5.9.3). One image serves main and the head only if the lockfile blobs are equal (prove it by `rev-parse` of both). **Budget (write it at Step 0): baseline file 1, base group 1, head file x3 plus rows alone 3 plus TZ 1, head group 1, mutant battery about 60 database-container starts (one `apione.sh` call per mutant, as the PR #98 and builder runs did; each behind the load gate), unit chain 1, scratch typecheck 1; image builds 2 at most.** Remove ONLY your own `pc-b864-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

