## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site** (your containers are local, no published port). Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` against a container you did not create (the copied `dbtest.sh` execs into the database container it created itself). Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, the in-process Jira GET of C7, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh pr comment`, `gh pr merge`, `gh pr edit` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add and merge-tree only inside `.tools/b864/repo` and `.tools/wt-b864-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders; the unit step's SOW text input is passed only as a read-only bind mount into a `--network none` container at the path `unit.sh` names (`PC_E8_SOW_TEXT`), `[ -f ]` only, never opened, printed, grepped, hashed or quoted. No Jira write (the C7 read is `get` only). No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test and the in-process read of the project's Jira client, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`): quarantine to `.tools/b864/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); write `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=` (a separator line is `echo ----`); multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII. Scratch changes (mutants, planted rows, planted copies of the test) live ONLY in `wt-b864-mut`, a container's own layer and `.tools/b864/scratch/`; never in the PR tree and never in a file of the shared repo. Synthetic data only. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"; do not quote git author fields), no card slug, clock from `date`. Nothing to any human. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (your STATUS carries a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read of the builder lane (B857 STATUS and commission), the earlier gate of this test (B828 and its two evidence files) and what you reuse; a READY-class verdict without one is returned); no message to any human; Jira writes none; never delete (quarantine). **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths; next commands; every scratch tree and mutant with its restore proof; lock released), stop your processes and containers, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". **Usage pause:** a session ended by the weekly limit is the platform, not a STOP; on resume re-read your STATUS last line, re-pin main, the head and the checks, and carry on against the hard stop Tuesday names in an addendum.

