## LANDING (Tuesday's, not the gate's; the gate quotes it in FOR TUESDAY and never runs it)
Composer lands by SQUASH, head-pinned, after the gate says GO or GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS and a real green scan of the head through the org ruleset (never bypassed, no alert dismissed). Source (the project's recorded practice for Composer code; the repo allows squash, merge commit and rebase): `1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md` line 1799 (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER, `sed -n 1799p`): "squash-merges PR #88 pinned to head 2da99cab after re-reading CodeQL and the checks. Nothing is deployed (Composer deploys only on your card)." The Composer project `CLAUDE.md` says the live demo site is the owner's: never deploy to it without the owner's word.
**Tuesday writes the squash subject AND body explicitly** (earlier Composer squashes carried a machine-local identity trailer; the branch commit here has none, MEASURED, but the text is still written, not defaulted) and lands with:
`gh pr merge 100 -R datasecau/Datasec-Security-Composer --squash --match-head-commit 9494afe71cdbafcf6b26e35d3e0d66b9cb2a2a3d --subject '<subject> (#100)' --body-file <f>`
- **Subject:** the commit title, `Date rule: three rows for an underscore after the year, after the month and inside the year (#100)` (or the wording Tuesday settles from the gate's C5/G-4 grade of the `describe`/year-row wording, which does not change the commit; the PR title is a public label only once the subject is explicit).
- **Body file `<f>`:** the paragraph of the commit message as the gate prints it at C5 ("A separator typed to take an underscore, or the year digit class typed to take an underscore, passed every test, so a date such as 2027_01-01 or 202_-01-01 could pass the pattern. Three rows now send an underscore after the year, after the month and inside the year through the refused-date helper, each on the same field as the neighbouring rows; each of those edits is red on a row. No product code changed."), then ONE attribution line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` and **no other trailer**. No person's name, no ticket key, no work number in the body (the PR body's key-free text stays in the PR). If the gate's C2c K-Y shows a year class taking `_` at the first, second or third place green, Tuesday decides before landing whether the sentence "the year digit class typed to take an underscore ... each of those edits is red on a row" needs "in the fourth place" (a wording change to the body file, not to the commit).
- **Verify after the merge, before anything else is done with main:** `gh api -X GET repos/datasecau/Datasec-Security-Composer/commits/<squash sha> --jq .commit.message` (GET only): (i) `/usr/bin/grep -c -i 'co-authored-by'` = 1 and the one line is the noreply address; (ii) `/usr/bin/grep -c -i 'localdomain'` = **0** (control: the same read on `cbe86ba61a45ed776122bf4ee31fd682a0244c1a` prints 1, MEASURED); (iii) the subject is the one written; (iv) the squash commit's parent is the main that was merged against and **its tree equals the head's tree `233405002b17f786fb67763bbfb9ccc57fd0969b`** while main is `304507b5` (if another PR landed first on other paths the tree differs by those paths, not by a conflict). **If (ii) is not 0 do not amend or rewrite main** (no force, no history edit): report it to the product owner as a finding about the landing and stop.
- A merge to main is not a deploy and Composer deploys only on the product owner's card. The records seat moves PCOMP-105 and files the YP1-YP3 residue as a later card if Tuesday decides so.
